 "notes": "PRIMARY SOURCE: the operator's own scorecard scan at victoriaparkgolf.com (https://victoriaparkgolf.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Scorecard-1.jpg), which prints all three nines (The Lakes, The Pines, The Valley) side by side plus the slope/rating block. Every yardage below was read off that scan and checksummed against the printed OUT totals (all 9 tee-set totals reconcile exactly). TEE SETS: only three - Blue, White, Red. There is no black/gold/championship tee. PAR: each nine is par 31, so every 18-hole combination is par 62. This is an EXECUTIVE-LENGTH course (Blue tees ~3,950-3,994 yards for 18); do not confuse it with a full-length card. STROKE INDEX: the club card prints 'H.C. STRKS M/L' as a 1-9 index within each nine, men/ladies. The 'handicap' field on each hole is the men's 1-9 index; 'handicapLadies' is the ladies' 1-9 index. 'handicap18Derived' is NOT printed on the club card - it is the standard odd-front / even-back expansion of the 9-hole indices, included only for convenience. GolfPass independently publishes exactly this expansion for the Lakes and Pines nines, which corroborates the derivation, but treat it as derived. RATINGS: the card gives slope/rating only for the three 18-hole combinations (Lakes/Pines, Lakes/Valley, Pines/Valley), never for a single nine, so per-nine rating/slope are null. Card prints them as Slope/Rating; they are stored here as separate 'slope' and 'rating' fields, men's on 'rating'/'slope' and women's on 'ratingLadies'/'slopeLadies'. Top-level 'teeSets'/'holes' mirror the Lakes/Pines combination purely to satisfy the requested flat shape; the authoritative per-nine data is under 'nines' and all three combos under 'combinations'. CROSS-CHECKS: Lakes nine - GolfPass Lakes page matches all 27 yardages, par and (expanded) handicaps, and matches the Lakes/Pines slope/rating for all three tees; mScorecard also matches the Lakes yardages. Pines nine - GolfPass Pines page matches all 27 yardages, par and handicaps, and reports 59.6/96, 58.8/94, 57.5/82, i.e. the card's Pines/Valley men's numbers. Valley nine - golfify.io matches all 27 yardages, par, and BOTH the men's and ladies' 1-9 stroke indices exactly. No numeric disagreement was found between the official card and any cross-check. KNOWN BAD SOURCES: mScorecard's entry titled 'Victoria Park Valley Golf Club - Lakes/Pines' is wrong - it repeats the Lakes nine twice as both front and back (total 3946 rather than 3950) and carries no stroke indices. GolfPass's 'Valley Course' page shows a hole table that is actually the LAKES nine. Both are conflation errors; the club's own card is authoritative. DISAMBIGUATION: this is Victoria Park VALLEY (7660 Maltby Rd. E, Puslinch), built 2012 to replace the former Victoria Park West. It is a different facility from Victoria Park EAST (1096 Victoria Rd. S), which shares the victoriaparkgolf.com website - do not mix their scorecards. CURRENCY: the scan was published in 2018 and is the newest card the operator has posted; yardages could have shifted slightly since, and the ratings predate any recent re-rating."
